# 🐳️ Build-context exclusions for 🌎️hub/Dockerfile (see its header).
# Only host-local state and compiler output that the builder stage recreates. Committed `🤖️generated`
# sources are NOT excluded — several crates and the plugin catalog are generated-then-committed, and
# dropping them would break the build inside the image. `.🧬semio` is the repository's host-local state
# root: the shared cargo cache (hundreds of GiB), hub data roots and tickets — none of it is a build
# input, and sending it made the context larger than the disk the build runs on. Patterns without `**/`
# match at the context root only, so every per-package output directory is excluded at any depth. The `dist`, staging
# (`📤️distribution`, `🔌️plugin-modules`, `🧩️extension-modules`, `📺️renderer-modules`) and wasm-pack (`pkg`) directories are
# git-ignored build outputs that no clean checkout has, and `♻️mit-bestand/🔎️recherche` is a research submodule no build
# reads: together they were ~14 GB of the ~23 GB context the first cold build started to send.
.git
.jj
.nx
.venv
.cursor
.🧬semio
.tmp*
**/node_modules
**/target
**/🎯️target
**/🎯️target-*
**/📤️dist
**/temp
**/test-results
**/storybook-static
**/🗑️generated
**/dist
**/📤️distribution
**/🔌️plugin-modules
**/🧩️extension-modules
**/📺️renderer-modules
**/pkg
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
♻️mit-bestand/🔎️recherche
**/.DS_Store
